# Decision Task Lifecycle

Purpose:
  Link decisions to tasks and track implementation progress.

Lifecycle:
  proposed
    -> task_created
    -> in_progress
    -> completed
    -> verified
    -> closed

  rejected
    -> archived

  superseded
    -> archived

Mapping:
  DEC-<ID> -> TASK-<ID>, TASK-<ID>, TASK-<ID>

Task Creation:
  When decision approved:
    1. Create tasks in .sdd/project/tasks/
    2. Link tasks to decision ID
    3. Assign chain type
    4. Set dependencies

Task Tracking:
  Each task references:
    - decision_id: DEC-<ID>
    - decision_title: <Decision Title>
    - chain: default

Verification:
  When task completes:
    1. Update decision status to implemented
    2. Run verification criteria
    3. Update decision status to verified or rejected

Rules:
  [DTL1] Every approved decision MUST create at least one task.
  [DTL2] Every task MUST reference its parent decision.
  [DTL3] Decision status MUST update as tasks progress.
  [DTL4] Verification MUST run before decision is closed.
  [DTL5] Superseded decisions MUST migrate tasks to new decision.

State: +
